WEBVTT

00:00:11.850 --> 00:00:13.820
Evan, where are you going?

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:14.740
Evan!

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:16.920
Evan, wait!

00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:20.440
Wait!

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:21.870
Take me with you!

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:22.800
Evan!

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:27.790
A dream...

00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:33.200
I just came to call you for dinner.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:34.270
Are you okay?

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:40.010
Right, I'm...

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:42.620
at a mage's home.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:50.010
<b>The Boy from the West and the Knight of the Blue Storm</b>

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:53.410
Time to eat.

00:01:00.810 --> 00:01:03.030
No need to worry, just eat.

00:01:08.410 --> 00:01:09.380
What?

00:01:10.010 --> 00:01:11.020
Oh, nothing...

00:01:13.950 --> 00:01:17.690
Ruth, I don't think he's seen 
you in that form before.

00:01:17.690 --> 00:01:18.660
Oh.

00:01:29.870 --> 00:01:32.320
Silky's cooking is delicious.

00:01:33.220 --> 00:01:36.370
Stare...

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:36.360
O-Okay.

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:53.230
Is there more bread, Mom?

00:02:04.630 --> 00:02:05.630
Um...

00:02:05.630 --> 00:02:09.310
I was just wondering if Mom 
and Dad are eating properly.

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:13.060
Your substitute should be handling it well.

00:02:14.010 --> 00:02:15.150
Oh.

00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:18.310
Do you miss home?

00:02:18.310 --> 00:02:20.210
I-It's nothing like that.

00:02:20.580 --> 00:02:23.430
Let's set out as soon as 
we're done with dinner.

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:26.790
We can't be too late.

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:32.540
We just have to take that horse and knight 
to the hill and return them to the Wild Hunt.

00:02:36.310 --> 00:02:39.340
I'm going to go talk to 
Evan before we leave.

00:02:39.340 --> 00:02:40.350
Gabriel...

00:02:40.570 --> 00:02:41.640
Don't worry.

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:43.300
I'll keep my distance.

00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:54.030
Hey.

00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:04.460
That's important to you, isn't it, friend?

00:03:06.550 --> 00:03:07.990
Thanks.

00:03:07.990 --> 00:03:09.640
Aren't you going to wear it?

00:03:10.220 --> 00:03:11.530
I'll put it on later.

00:03:11.910 --> 00:03:14.300
Also, stop calling me that.

00:03:16.220 --> 00:03:18.300
You are my friend, are you not?

00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:21.340
I am, but...

00:03:22.670 --> 00:03:24.510
<i>You should call me Gabe.</i>

00:03:24.510 --> 00:03:25.140
<i>Gabe.</i>

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:31.530
Call me Gabe. Like you should.

00:03:37.270 --> 00:03:38.660
All right.

00:03:38.660 --> 00:03:40.230
I'll make an effort going forward.

00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:42.870
Going forward?

00:03:43.460 --> 00:03:45.140
I thought this was the end.

00:03:46.420 --> 00:03:49.710
My role is to guide the weather.

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:55.640
Once we return to our flow, a new 
season will come to this land.

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:03.600
What the hell?

00:04:04.060 --> 00:04:05.560
That makes no sense.

00:04:24.170 --> 00:04:26.270
Gabriel, we should get...

00:04:28.880 --> 00:04:30.380
Already?

00:04:30.380 --> 00:04:32.020
Just a little longer.

00:04:34.550 --> 00:04:38.330
I'd rather not take a child like you.

00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:40.060
You're feeble.

00:04:40.060 --> 00:04:42.590
Creatures that are already close to death

00:04:42.590 --> 00:04:45.230
are more susceptible to being 
dragged to the other side.

00:04:47.170 --> 00:04:49.580
What happens if I am?

00:04:50.360 --> 00:04:53.220
It'll be all right, as long 
as we can see him off.

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:08.740
It may seem odd to wear these during the 
summer solstice, but it might be for the better.

00:05:09.480 --> 00:05:11.550
Thanks, Silver.

00:05:27.480 --> 00:05:29.850
The wind feels damp.

00:05:29.850 --> 00:05:32.360
Tonight might be the last storm.

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:35.700
Evan...

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:38.710
Don't.

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:40.740
Let me go!

00:05:43.550 --> 00:05:44.430
No.

00:06:02.540 --> 00:06:04.820
Nothing's happening.

00:06:11.250 --> 00:06:12.040
Chise.

00:06:12.040 --> 00:06:12.620
Yeah.

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:36.260
Forgive my late arrival, my king.

00:06:46.370 --> 00:06:49.200
I've been looking for you, Leader.

00:06:50.980 --> 00:06:52.080
Is that...

00:06:52.480 --> 00:06:53.660
Yeah.

00:06:53.660 --> 00:06:55.890
The ones who runs through stormy fields.

00:06:55.890 --> 00:06:57.640
Wild Hunt.

00:06:57.640 --> 00:06:58.690
Knights...

00:06:59.920 --> 00:07:01.760
That's an order of chivalry.

00:07:02.250 --> 00:07:04.410
Evan was a knight.

00:07:05.380 --> 00:07:06.690
Gabriel...

00:07:12.690 --> 00:07:13.660
No!

00:07:15.780 --> 00:07:18.460
You shouldn't go near that fog.

00:07:18.460 --> 00:07:19.910
But, Gabriel...

00:07:22.170 --> 00:07:25.580
You, who have been freed from the yoke...

00:07:26.290 --> 00:07:31.290
We will now become the storm 
and return to where we belong.

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:33.460
The time is here!

00:07:35.450 --> 00:07:36.400
Evan.

00:07:42.230 --> 00:07:43.880
Where are you going?

00:07:45.450 --> 00:07:47.270
Anywhere.

00:07:47.270 --> 00:07:49.790
We run free through the night.

00:07:50.500 --> 00:07:51.590
Free...

00:07:53.270 --> 00:07:54.910
I want to run, too.

00:07:56.030 --> 00:07:59.300
Held back by no one. Free.

00:08:01.740 --> 00:08:04.470
Take me with you.

00:08:07.930 --> 00:08:09.070
Let's go!

00:08:23.220 --> 00:08:25.120
My body feels lighter.

00:08:26.380 --> 00:08:28.140
Let's go after them, Elias.

00:08:33.400 --> 00:08:35.580
Well, off we go.

00:08:36.120 --> 00:08:36.900
Okay.

00:08:43.270 --> 00:08:45.120
No one's here to stop me.

00:08:45.120 --> 00:08:46.750
I'm free!

00:09:03.420 --> 00:09:05.300
Wow!

00:09:08.280 --> 00:09:09.560
Gabriel!

00:09:13.230 --> 00:09:15.590
Can we get close enough to reach him?

00:09:15.590 --> 00:09:16.500
All right.

00:09:31.140 --> 00:09:32.370
Don't go.

00:09:40.590 --> 00:09:41.720
Gabriel!

00:09:52.810 --> 00:09:54.180
Elias...

00:09:54.180 --> 00:09:55.440
Why?

00:09:55.440 --> 00:09:56.600
Look at that.

00:09:58.340 --> 00:09:59.460
That's...

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:05.050
You would have been in 
danger if they'd hit you.

00:10:05.050 --> 00:10:06.600
I think that's enough.

00:10:06.600 --> 00:10:09.470
Maybe he'll be happiest with them.

00:10:10.960 --> 00:10:14.260
But Gabriel has a family waiting for him.

00:10:16.800 --> 00:10:18.530
Oh, all right...

00:10:22.290 --> 00:10:24.970
Wow, we've already come so far!

00:10:25.800 --> 00:10:27.200
Look!

00:10:27.840 --> 00:10:30.820
Up ahead is the gem shop
 I used to go to all the time.

00:10:30.820 --> 00:10:35.240
Even further up there is my school 
and the apartment I lived at.

00:10:35.240 --> 00:10:36.770
And over there...

00:10:39.820 --> 00:10:41.080
Over there...

00:10:44.080 --> 00:10:45.810
36.8.

00:10:45.810 --> 00:10:47.360
Looks like you're all right.

00:11:02.100 --> 00:11:03.880
Gabriel...

00:11:03.880 --> 00:11:05.370
I hope he's all right.

00:11:12.540 --> 00:11:14.230
They changed direction.

00:11:16.430 --> 00:11:17.440
A hospital.

00:11:26.110 --> 00:11:27.070
Mom...

00:11:29.250 --> 00:11:30.580
Gabriel!

00:11:35.880 --> 00:11:36.840
Ow.

00:11:39.250 --> 00:11:40.260
Huh?

00:11:40.260 --> 00:11:41.160
I...

00:11:48.470 --> 00:11:49.540
Elias...

00:11:49.540 --> 00:11:50.740
Gabriel is...

00:11:51.270 --> 00:11:54.230
It looks like he's free from 
the Wild Hunt's spell.

00:11:54.230 --> 00:11:55.320
Let's go.

00:12:10.550 --> 00:12:11.400
E-Evan.

00:12:13.230 --> 00:12:15.000
It's a fantastic journey, is it not?

00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:16.220
Y-Yeah.

00:12:16.700 --> 00:12:19.040
It's awesome and all, but...

00:12:20.230 --> 00:12:22.400
I was just wondering how far we're going.

00:12:25.190 --> 00:12:26.930
To where we belong.

00:12:28.390 --> 00:12:30.070
Where we belong?

00:12:30.630 --> 00:12:31.390
Yes.

00:12:31.970 --> 00:12:33.690
Is that still far away?

00:12:34.190 --> 00:12:34.950
Yes.

00:12:35.630 --> 00:12:37.630
I should...

00:12:37.630 --> 00:12:39.290
Don't worry.

00:12:40.290 --> 00:12:45.240
To be with us is to be at peace.

00:12:47.260 --> 00:12:49.870
Creatures that are already close to death

00:12:49.870 --> 00:12:52.280
are more susceptible to being 
dragged to the other side.

00:12:53.620 --> 00:12:56.190
Do you mean...

00:12:58.080 --> 00:12:59.380
I'm dying?

00:13:01.480 --> 00:13:04.200
The death of the flesh is insignificant.

00:13:04.200 --> 00:13:05.850
Together, we'll run through the night.

00:13:06.300 --> 00:13:09.180
We'll hear the blackbird's song 
in the shadows of the stars.

00:13:09.660 --> 00:13:12.300
We'll nap through the morning fog.

00:13:12.560 --> 00:13:15.810
We'll all be together from now on,

00:13:16.220 --> 00:13:17.230
Gabe.

00:13:19.380 --> 00:13:20.670
Gabriel!

00:13:22.150 --> 00:13:23.420
Gabriel!

00:13:23.420 --> 00:13:24.160
Get down!

00:13:25.150 --> 00:13:26.450
The mage—

00:13:27.690 --> 00:13:30.200
If I am your friend,

00:13:30.600 --> 00:13:33.450
I shall be your eternal friend.

00:13:34.710 --> 00:13:35.810
No.

00:13:36.330 --> 00:13:37.970
What I wanted...

00:13:38.760 --> 00:13:41.690
It wasn't this... It wasn't like this.

00:13:42.860 --> 00:13:48.120
Elias, how can we pull Gabriel 
away from the Wild Hunt?

00:13:48.120 --> 00:13:51.470
First, we'll have to stop 
that horse and knight.

00:13:53.570 --> 00:13:54.950
I'll deal with the horse.

00:13:55.380 --> 00:13:57.710
I'll take the knight, then.

00:13:58.840 --> 00:14:00.340
Thank you.

00:14:01.280 --> 00:14:05.320
That said, it'll be up to him in the end.

00:14:07.690 --> 00:14:10.230
My friend, are you having fun?

00:14:13.270 --> 00:14:14.230
I'm sorry.

00:14:15.640 --> 00:14:18.100
I can't go with you.

00:14:19.970 --> 00:14:22.520
I did have fun.

00:14:23.510 --> 00:14:28.720
Being friends with you and 
flying through the sky like this...

00:14:29.180 --> 00:14:32.160
I've always wanted to 
do something like this.

00:14:33.660 --> 00:14:38.920
If it weren't for my body, I wouldn't 
have had to move to the countryside.

00:14:39.520 --> 00:14:41.430
I would have made friends right away.

00:14:41.430 --> 00:14:44.550
We'd run around and
 play soccer and stuff.

00:14:45.280 --> 00:14:49.600
No one would tell me to 
wear this stupid thing.

00:14:49.600 --> 00:14:52.270
Mom and Dad wouldn't have to deal with me.

00:14:52.930 --> 00:14:56.370
They wouldn't have to look so tired.

00:14:57.110 --> 00:15:02.120
I've always wished my 
body weren't like this.

00:15:03.820 --> 00:15:06.850
You have nothing to worry 
about anymore, then.

00:15:06.850 --> 00:15:10.620
From now until this planet perishes, 
we'll be together as we run,

00:15:10.620 --> 00:15:12.550
as we sleep, and as we—

00:15:12.550 --> 00:15:13.270
But...

00:15:15.010 --> 00:15:17.770
But you know...

00:15:18.740 --> 00:15:20.800
I still...

00:15:23.930 --> 00:15:26.490
I want to go home.

00:15:38.530 --> 00:15:39.570
What is this?

00:15:39.890 --> 00:15:41.060
Sorry.

00:15:46.190 --> 00:15:48.060
Gabriel! Jump!

00:15:48.300 --> 00:15:50.110
I promise I'll catch you!

00:16:21.290 --> 00:16:22.580
Are you all right?

00:16:24.200 --> 00:16:26.020
Y-Yeah.

00:16:27.670 --> 00:16:29.270
They're going home.

00:16:38.720 --> 00:16:39.820
Gabriel...

00:16:42.590 --> 00:16:43.600
Are you okay?

00:16:47.980 --> 00:16:49.610
Th-Thanks.

00:16:54.840 --> 00:16:56.110
That was scary, huh?

00:17:01.430 --> 00:17:03.700
It was kinda fun, though.

00:17:04.590 --> 00:17:06.800
I felt like I could go on forever.

00:17:06.800 --> 00:17:09.530
I sort of thought... that didn't sound too bad.

00:17:11.030 --> 00:17:14.900
I think I know what you mean.

00:17:16.890 --> 00:17:21.220
But I'm glad you're back.

00:17:22.600 --> 00:17:25.410
Welcome back, Gabriel.

00:17:31.390 --> 00:17:33.460
Chise, how are your chills?

00:17:33.460 --> 00:17:35.680
I'm a bit warm, if anything.

00:17:35.680 --> 00:17:36.720
Good.

00:17:42.220 --> 00:17:45.500
Why do you think they let Gabriel go?

00:17:46.070 --> 00:17:50.260
They rarely let go of 
anything they've pulled in.

00:17:50.930 --> 00:17:55.860
It might be that something 
with a will got in their way.

00:18:29.220 --> 00:18:30.410
I'm home.

00:18:42.030 --> 00:18:44.530
Looks like they figured things out.

00:18:48.840 --> 00:18:51.390
The new season's here, too.

00:18:54.310 --> 00:18:56.940
It was here when I woke up this morning.

00:18:57.590 --> 00:19:00.130
I suppose this is their 
idea of compensation.

00:19:09.390 --> 00:19:11.720
Looks like we're having a feast every night.

00:19:13.020 --> 00:19:15.120
We're always having a feast.

00:19:19.120 --> 00:19:21.720
Are you sure you don't 
need me to come with you?

00:19:21.720 --> 00:19:23.650
I said I'll be okay.

00:19:23.650 --> 00:19:25.050
I'm going now.

00:19:26.460 --> 00:19:28.060
Gabriel...

00:19:30.610 --> 00:19:31.470
What?

00:19:34.980 --> 00:19:36.130
Stay safe.

00:19:36.130 --> 00:19:37.610
I know.

00:19:37.610 --> 00:19:38.960
See you later.

00:22:11.660 --> 00:22:12.880
How do I look?

00:22:13.590 --> 00:22:15.960
It looks to be just the right size for you.

00:22:16.520 --> 00:22:18.090
Is it comfortable?

00:22:18.660 --> 00:22:20.120
It's perfect.

00:22:21.290 --> 00:22:22.480
But...

00:22:22.480 --> 00:22:23.980
Thank you.

00:22:25.530 --> 00:22:28.890
For being understanding 
about me going to college.

00:22:29.280 --> 00:22:31.430
It was your decision.

00:22:37.160 --> 00:22:39.250
I wonder what it's like there.
